            { q: "What is RFM analysis?", opts: ["Revenue, Finance, Marketing", "Recency (last purchase), Frequency (purchase count), Monetary (total spend) — customer value segmentation", "A statistical regression", "A type of cohort"], a: 1, exp: "RFM scores customers on three dimensions. High RFM customers are your best customers. Low RFM are at-risk or churned. Enables targeted marketing." },
            { q: "What is Customer Lifetime Value (CLV)?", opts: ["Revenue from one purchase", "Total net revenue expected from a customer over their entire relationship with the company", "Annual subscription value", "Average order value"], a: 1, exp: "CLV guides acquisition spend decisions: if CLV is $500, spending $100 to acquire a customer is profitable. CLV = Average Purchase Value × Frequency × Customer Lifespan." }
