            { q: "What is a moving average used for?", opts: ["Averaging multiple models", "Smoothing time series by replacing each value with the average of surrounding values — revealing underlying trend", "A type of forecasting model", "Calculating the mean"], a: 1, exp: "7-day moving average smooths out daily noise to reveal weekly trends. 4-week moving average smooths weekly variation to reveal monthly trends." },
            { q: "What is autocorrelation?", opts: ["Correlation between two different time series", "Correlation of a time series with its own past values — yesterday's sales predicting today's sales", "A forecasting error metric", "Correlation between variables"], a: 1, exp: "Autocorrelation captures temporal dependency. Stock prices, website traffic, and weather are autocorrelated — past values help predict future values." },
            { q: "What is Prophet (Facebook) used for?", opts: ["Social media analytics", "A time series forecasting tool designed for business data with strong seasonality and holiday effects", "A data pipeline tool", "A visualization library"], a: 1, exp: "Prophet handles business time series: trend + yearly/weekly seasonality + holiday effects. It's robust to missing data and outliers — popular for business forecasting." },
            { q: "What is time series decomposition?", opts: ["Breaking a time series into multiple datasets", "Separating a time series into trend, seasonal, and residual components for analysis", "A data cleaning technique", "Splitting time series for train/test"], a: 1, exp: "Decomposition reveals structure: trend (long-term direction), seasonality (repeating patterns), and residuals (random noise). Each component can be analyzed independently." }
